# Optimizer boundaries

- Validate all IR before scans, rewriting or unreachable-function removal.
- Inline only bounded, structurally eligible closed bodies. Keep recursive SCCs
  as calls; alpha-rename callee locals and bind every argument once in order,
  including unused arguments with rejection, overflow, SHA or divergence.
- Charge optional expansion before copying. Retry the preceding optimized IR
  only for private typed lowering limits; never mask validation, Rue or internal
  errors. Keep existing limits and the unoptimized route.
- Preserve evaluation mode through public optimize/serialize/recompile. Without
  an independent wire-mode field, retain original runtime IR when mode removal
  leaves a possibly failing result. The closed total-result whitelist runs only
  after validation; check every constructor/branch child. Private compilation
  separately pins the original runtime mode.
- A legacy comparison can schedule operands differently from runtime lowering.
  Use executed typed failures to test this: Eq(Raise, AtomValue(First(input)))
  distinguishes source-left-first Raise from legacy InvalidOpArg on nil input.
- Keep Rue codegen iterative, including static-data traversal and staged Closure
  emission. Preserve child/allocator order and repeated DAG allocation. Exercise
  default-sized thread stacks; raising a test's stack is not a robustness fix.
- Propagate integer bounds only on immutable lexical values after successful
  guards. Join successful paths and start fresh callee scopes; never borrow
  sibling/future facts. Discard checked arithmetic only when proven total.
- Forward runtime first/rest aliases only under the corresponding branch-local
  pair fact. Track physical binding generations, resolve paths at the final
  consumer and start fresh callee scopes. Retain strict captures otherwise.
  Preflight all bodies and bound analysis, descriptors, reuse and path distance;
  retry a fresh preceding emitter on private typed optional limits. Do not
  generalize this to the disabled backward runtime guard-removal pass.
- Preserve scalar/length/canonicality/range/body decoder order. Nil is canonical
  zero; nonempty canonical integers lie in unsigned byte interval [0080,ff80).
  The independent Seq8 law does not prove opcode/ABI/compiler preservation.
- Measure serialized bytes together with VM work. Full bundle cost needs actual
  consensus measurements; tiny constant hashes can increase generator byte cost.
- Keep historical snapshots immutable and signed/unsigned status explicit.
  Validate the active append/composition source, native and typed evidence plus
  complete fresh Cargo bundles before pure historical projection. Never validate
  restored history as current source. Preserve historical source-only labels and
  six downloads. Follow current-evidence.mdc and the active append/composition
  gates; the old guarded profile remains pending. Run the existing
  helper/refinement/cost gates with retained VM replay. Conditions-helper
  runs skip BLS verification and do not add SDK admissions. Resource failures remain
  inconclusive; finite savings are not universal dominance or compiler preservation.
